d 15. Electrical Basic only is Basic Electronics. Science Math only is read as both Mathematics rows. Cowboy, Rogue and Wilderness are printed None and left out. || MONEY: 1D4x1000 dollars in personal savings stored (printed lD4x$1000; Australian dollars equal credits). The monthly salary of 2,000 rising 200 per level and the discounts on rent, tax, food and medical costs are in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: citizen card reader and badge and identification have no row. The headset radio and notebook computer use the nearest catalog rows. The riot issue (full flak vest with helmet and riot shield, or a full suit of light to medium environmental armor of 50-75 M.D.C.) is issued only in combat or riot situations and is in GM Notes, as are the patrol cruiser, the Security Commando powered armor suit and the M.D. rifles issued for assaults. The book lists the S.D.C. pistol or submachinegun, the Super-10 shotgun, the M-01 and the 20K Tazer and then says an officer usually carries one S.D.C. and one M.D. handgun; all four are stored. || NOT STORED: The Law Code table (item and section codes) is setting. Rank (starts as a Corporal) is in GM Notes."
