## Lore

The City Police keep the peace inside the walls of Melbourne and Perth.
They are a disciplined, loyal and well organized service, separate from the
military police but often working beside them on security, terrorists and
rogue mutants. Cadets are drilled like soldiers and trained in firearms,
driving, hand to hand combat, surveillance and intelligence work, and also
in etiquette, courtesy and immaculate dress: light gray with black trim in
Melbourne, dark blue with black trim in Perth.

Most officers joined out of a sense of justice and care about the people
they serve. They do not write the laws, though, and they enforce them to
the letter, trusting their superiors and the Central Computer and seldom
disobeying an order. Every lapse is recorded and punished, from demerits
and fines up to demotion, loss of citizen level, prison, exile or
execution. That makes them stern, and a minority enjoy it; the bullies with
the best arrest records tend to rise.

Citizens respect them and help them readily. Outside the walls it is a
different matter: Outbackers have no rights in the City''s eyes, and police
pursuing a criminal or a lead there can be far more ruthless without fear
of consequences.

## GM Notes

Authority: in uniform an officer is treated as slightly above a Level 4
citizen. He may enter restricted areas, access sensitive information and
give orders to citizens; refusal is code 17D, disobeying an officer.

Most police are regional and ill-suited to long adventures far from base.
A wandering officer is usually an undercover agent or special investigator,
an exile, or a deserter. Investigations of more than 12 hours outside the
City need permission.

Issue the sheet does not list: a citizen card reader, badge and
identification. In combat or riot situations, a full flak vest with helmet
and riot shield, or a full suit of light to medium environmental M.D.C.
armor (typically 50-75 M.D.C.). Officers usually carry one S.D.C. and one
M.D. handgun; M.D. rifles and other weapons are kept in patrol vehicles or
assigned for assaults and the defence of the City. A patrol cruiser (380
M.D.C., 180 mph/288 km, radio and onboard computer, no weapons) or a
Security Commando powered armor suit is issued. Permits for non-issue
weapons exist and are easily revoked.

Pay and perks: $2,000 a month, rising $200 per level if conduct is good;
40% off rent and city taxes (or a precinct dormitory), 20% off food and 50%
off medical costs, with line-of-duty injuries treated free. Savings are
1D4x1000 dollars. Australian dollars equal credits.

Rank: starts as a Corporal, with the same ranks as the military. Sergeant,
lieutenant, detective lieutenant and captain are the most common.

Cybernetics: 30% of officers have 1D4 cybernetics of choice and 10% have
minor partial bionics, or prosthetics as needed.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'city-police-australia');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'city-police-australia';

